  "klappen_headline": "Three generations. A concealed breach. A land the sea reclaims.",
  "klappentext": "Sankt Annen, 1906: on the night of the great storm tide the dyke breaks at a weak spot that Hauke Carstens, as dyke-reeve, was responsible for. A neighbour drowns – and Hauke conceals that he knew the spot was faulty and, to save money, had left it unrepaired. The breach becomes an accident, the silence an inheritance.\n\nAcross three generations the family carries the guilt, embanked like the land itself – through two wars, land reform and the economic miracle – until the granddaughter Wiebke returns as a coastal engineer and the rising sea lays bare the old foreland that was once drowned.\n\nA sober, epic coastal drama about guilt and silence, land and water – and what remains when the sea reclaims what was wrested from it.",
